hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23612","Ismail ya'ni Ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Husayn ibn Dhakwan narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah from Abdullah ibn Muhammad from a woman among them, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me while I was eating with my left, and I was a left-handed woman, so he struck my hand and the morsel fell, and he said: Do not eat with your left, and Allah has made for you a right; or he said: And Allah has freed your right. She said: So my left turned into a right, and I never ate with it afterwards."
